__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
evidence/*.log
.env
node_modules/
web/dist/
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
web/compare/
web/dist-ssr/
web/.wrangler/
.commitmsg
# Written by the coverage floor the door enforces at step 7. Untracked, it dirties the tree
# and push.sh refuses to push - the gate blocking its own door on the gate's own artefact.
.coverage
# T-S6. The project's own writable root: the concurrency lock `scripts/run_budgeted.sh` holds and
# the Q-M2 output `scripts/measure_qm2.py` publishes. Both used to sit on fixed names in the
# host's shared /tmp, where the ten projects on this box can reach them. Ignored for the same
# reason `.coverage` is - it is generated, and an unignored generated file would make the door
# refuse its own tree. NOT to be removed by `git clean`, which is forbidden here anyway: unlinking
# the lock file while a run holds it releases the guarantee without any error.
.state/

# Backups of the environment file. `.env` itself was ignored; its copies were not, so a single
# `cp .env .env.bak` inside the tree would have staged every key in it. The neighbouring apibase
# repository carried this exact gap and closed it as A-02; closing it here too rather than
# trusting that nobody will ever make that copy.
.env.bak*
.env*.bak*
*.bak-*

# T-GL-04/D-63. The GenLayer CLI's default keystore file (`genlayer account create`) - GL-05's
# funded Studionet/Testnet Bradbury account lives in `~/orchestra/gl/`, never in this tree, but the
# pattern is added now rather than the day a `genlayer account create` is accidentally run from
# inside a checkout: an ignore rule added after a key was staged protects nothing that already
# happened, the same reasoning `.env.bak*` above was added for.
keypair.json

# `gltest` creates (and clears) this directory itself on every run - empty today, so `git status`
# does not see it (git does not track empty directories at all), but ignored proactively rather
# than waiting for the day a live/integration run writes a real compiled-contract artefact into it
# and the door refuses an otherwise-clean tree over a generated file nobody meant to commit.
integrations/genlayer-witness/artifacts/
